    {
      "id": "claim_0ba881cd4b07493095821e734d85b06f",
      "statement": "The runner enters the _io_for context manager once per stage inside the execution loop rather than once per run, so each stage receives a freshly built driver, writer and reader that are torn down before the next stage begins.",
